/// known-gap: interp has no block overlay syntax (overlay name ... xx); the interpreter is being retired
/// A `modify` line may read `intensity` and the host: it is worked out
/// again every tick, with the stored values (the film is not read back
/// into itself). Reading gives the stored value plus the film; a write
/// sets what reading gives, and the stored value is what is left when the
/// film comes off.
<>F |
    def: 10
xx
overlay fade
    decays: .25
    modify
        @def - @def * intensity / 2
    xx
xx
f <> F | def: 10
:overlay!(f, fade)
:say(f >> def)
:tick()
:say(f >> def)
f >> def |= f >> def + 1
:say(f >> def)
:tick()
:say(f >> def)
:tick()
:tick()
:say(f >> def)
